   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Is the pair shift S in the algebra of the t's?\n\nExpectation: t₁(θ_F) has P on F sites and (θ_F−θ_A) + hK on A sites; t₃(θ_A−h) has P on A sites and (θ_A−θ_F−4h) + hK on F sites. Their product should be S (or S⁻¹) times dressings (x + hK)(−x−4h + hK) = x(−x−4h)·1 (K² = 4K), x = θ_F − θ_A. So U = t₁(θ_F) t₃(θ_A−h) ∝ S for generic x, but U = 0 at **x = 0 (θ_A = θ_F, the point used so far)** and at x = −4h. At x = −2h both dressings are −2h + hK (Minahan–Zarembo's −2 + K): candidate ABJM point.\n\nTest on a random ψ, untwisted, pair-periodic θ (θ_F = 0): fit Uψ = c Sψ and Uψ = c S⁻¹ψ.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* use the reduced t3bar = tr[Lbar_1...Lbar_L Gbar] (no scalar prod g_s): t3 itself vanishes at theta_A - theta_F = 2h through g_F(theta_A - h) *)\nt3barV[ths_, G_, v_, psi_] := transferVec[barE, types, ths, N[Det[G] Transpose[Inverse[G]]], v, psi];\nshiftTest[thA_, thF_] := Module[{ths = Flatten[Table[{thA, thF}, Lp]], Ups, Sps, Sips, cS, cSi},\n   Ups = t1V[ths, G1, thF, t3barV[ths, G1, thA - hh, psiR]];\n   Sps = psiR[[perm]]; Sips = psiR[[InversePermutation[perm]]];\n   cS = (Conjugate[Sps] . Ups)/(Conjugate[Sps] . Sps); cSi = (Conjugate[Sips] . Ups)/(Conjugate[Sips] . Sips);\n   {thA - thF, Norm[Ups]/Norm[psiR], Norm[Ups - cS Sps]/Max[Norm[Ups], 10^-300], Norm[Ups - cSi Sips]/Max[Norm[Ups], 10^-300], Chop[cS], Chop[cSi]}];\nshiftRows = shiftTest[#, 0] & /@ {0, 2 hh, 0.3, -2 hh, 4 hh};\nGrid[Prepend[Map[If[NumericQ[#] && !ExactNumberQ[#], ScientificForm[#, 3], #] &, shiftRows, {2}],\n  {\"θ_A − θ_F\", \"‖Uψ‖/‖ψ‖,  U = t₁(θ_F) t̄₃(θ_A−h)\", \"U ∝ S? (rel res)\", \"U ∝ S⁻¹? (rel res)\", \"c (S)\", \"c (S⁻¹)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
