  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary (2026-10-12, L = 2 pairs)\n\n- **On-shell states [numeric]:** joint t₁, t₃ diagonalisation (vector t₃ from `dual-lax-t3.wb`) on HW ∩ cyclic reproduces the §5.7 table: [1,0,1] states C₁ = C₃ = 1/√8, 1/√24 (t₁ gap 10⁻¹⁶, joint gap 0.31), singlets C₂ = −1/√15, −1/4 (signs = phase convention).\n- **Why the old matching failed (two reasons):** (i) t₁ alone did not split the adjoint pair; (ii) even with t₃, the 1/√8 state is degenerate in **t₁, t₂, t₃** with an odd-momentum HW [1,0,1] state χ; only the pair translation S separates them. The inhomogeneous deformation θ = δθ⁰ breaks S and the limit is an S-mixture (overlap 0.9938, LHS → 0.3121).\n- **Fix:** pair-periodic θ (θ_A = δα, θ_F = δβ) and the **twisted shift Ŝ = S∘ρ_{3..L}(Λ)**, which commutes with t_a at finite twist (plain S does not; it gives O(ε) errors). Diagonalising t₁, t₃, Ŝ: overlap → 1, LHS → 1/√8 and 1/√24, odd-bridge formula exact (10⁻¹¹–10⁻¹³) at every ε, matched states exact eigenstates (10⁻¹⁵). The §5.7 caveat is resolved.\n- **Next:** L = 3 pairs (set `Lp = 3`): sectors are larger (the twisted-sector matrices are built column by column, cost ∝ sector dim × 0.16 s per t₃ pass).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
